      "metadata": {
        "title": "A counterexample on cyclic blocks in finitary permutation groups",
        "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21538908",
        "publication_date": "2026-07-24",
        "description": "<p>We give a negative answer to Kourovka Notebook Problem 21.6. &nbsp;Starting from a minimally transitive permutation \\(2\\)-group of degree eight with an explicit cycle-support obstruction, we form a restricted iterated imprimitive wreath limit. &nbsp;The result is a countable transitive totally imprimitive finitary \\(2\\)-group containing no transitive subgroup with the requested cyclic-block property.</p>\n<p>This manuscript addresses the intended mathematical problem identified in the source.</p>\n<p>AI disclosure: This problem was solved using GPT 5.6 Sol.</p>\n<p>Mathematics subject: math.GR; source problem: OP-0695.</p>",
